**Major find.** Chruściel 1992's actual formulation of SCC is:

> "Strong Cosmic Censorship Conjecture (SCCC): Every maximal Hausdorff development of a generic Cauchy data set (Σ, g, K), with (Σ, g) compact or asymptotically flat, is globally hyperbolic. This conjecture is often formulated in the C^{1,2}? context, and a breakdown of C^{1,2}... differentiability class of the metric on a globally hyperbolic manifold is considered as a breakdown of validity of the conjecture."

The OCR shows "Cf;:" and "C1~;" which are garbled — likely "C^2" or "C^{1,1}"? "often formulated in the C^2 context, and a breakdown of C^2 differentiability class of the metric on a globally hyperbolic manifold is considered as a breakdown of validity of the conjecture." The garbled "Cf;:" could be "C^2" — most likely "C^2" (OCR of superscript 2 as "f;"?). Hmm, "Cf;:" might be OCR of "C^2" (superscript 2 misread). And "C1~;" might be "C^2" again? Or "C^{1,1}"? Let me zoom in on the OCR text around those tokens to see. But the key content is unambiguous:
- SCCC = every maximal Hausdorff development of generic Cauchy data (compact or AF) is globally hyperbolic.
